{
  "id": 309709618,
  "iid": 16058,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "radius: Support $INCLUDEs with absolute paths",
  "description": "The FreeRADIUS parser allows absolute paths in its dictionary parser\n(cf. the man page for dictionary which implies it's a relative filename,\nhttps://freeradius.org/radiusd/man/dictionary.html, but the source\ncode in FreeRADIUS src/lib/util/dict_tokenize.c allows it.)\nSupport that as well for compatibility, and because some\nusers might find it useful to refer to files in a different\ndirectory than their personal configuration directory, especially\nsome shared location.\n\nMake sure to save the new directory so that relative $INCLUDEs within\nthe new file are handled, and to switch back.\n\nWe don't follow symlinks for handling subsequent relative INCLUDEs, as\nFreeRADIUS's parser doesn't either, but perhaps it would be useful.\n(Less necessary now that we handle absolute paths.)\n\nFix #6466",
